# SmartResume AI — System Architecture Document

Companion to `PRD.md` (what) and `AGENT.md` (process). Requirement IDs (AUTH-01, ATS-04 …) refer to the PRD. Where this document is more specific than the PRD, **this document is authoritative for implementation details**.

---

## 1. Architecture Overview

SmartResume AI is a **monorepo with three npm workspaces**:

| Workspace | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `client/` | React + TypeScript SPA (Vite). UI, editor state, templates, print page. |
| `server/` | Express + TypeScript REST API. Auth, resumes, AI, ATS, PDF. |
| `shared/` | TypeScript types, Zod schemas, constants (template list, limits), and the pure `calculateCompleteness()` function used by both sides. |

Runtime pieces: Browser SPA → REST API (`/api/v1`) → MongoDB Atlas; API → LLM provider (HTTPS); API → headless Chromium (local process) → SPA's `/print` route → API (print token).

## 2. Architecture Style & Justification

**Modular monolith** (one deployable backend, feature modules inside) + **SPA** frontend.

- One backend process keeps deployment, debugging and demoing simple for a mini project. Microservices would add networking, deployment and observability cost with zero benefit at this scale.
- Feature modules (`auth`, `users`, `resumes`, `ai`, `ats`, `jobmatch`, `pdf`, `templates`) each own routes → controller → service → model, so any module can later be extracted.
- Layering rule (backend): **routes → controllers (HTTP only) → services (business logic) → models (persistence)**. Controllers never touch Mongoose; services never touch `req/res`.
- The ATS engine is a **pure function library** (`engine/`) with no I/O, making it deterministic and trivially unit-testable.

