## 23. Scalability Considerations

Out of MVP scope but design-compatible: stateless API (horizontal scaling; move rate-limit stores to Redis); PDF rendering extractable into a worker/queue; sections embedded keeps reads to one document; indexes on `{userId, updatedAt}`; list endpoints paginated and projected; ATS engine pure and CPU-light; LLM provider abstraction allows switching vendors; analyses pruned to 10 per resume; static client served via CDN.

## 24. Technical Trade-offs

| Decision | Alternative | Why chosen / cost |
|---|---|---|
| Puppeteer PDF | `@react-pdf/renderer`; client `html2canvas` | Only approach with exact preview fidelity + selectable text with one set of templates. Cost: heavier hosting, hence print fallback. |
| Heuristic ATS engine | LLM-scored ATS | Deterministic, explainable, free, testable. Cost: not "real" ATS; disclaimer shown. |
| Embedded sections | Separate `sections` collection | One read/write, atomic autosave. Cost: whole-doc updates (small docs). |
| JWT access + refresh cookie | Server sessions | API stays stateless; refresh is revocable. Cost: more code than sessions. |
| Same-origin proxy | Cross-site cookies + CORS | Avoids Safari/Chrome third-party cookie blocking. Cost: host-specific rewrite config. |
| Plain-text bullets | Rich text editor | ATS-safe, simpler PDF/AI. Cost: no inline bold/links in bullets. |
| Zustand + Query | Redux Toolkit | Less boilerplate. |
| Task-based AI assistant | Free-form chat | Safer, testable, easier guardrails. Cost: less flexible. |
| Gemini default | OpenAI | Free tier for students; provider is swappable. |
| JD text not stored | Store JD | Privacy; cost: cannot re-display old JD (hash only). |
| No email flows in MVP | Nodemailer/Resend | Avoids external setup; listed as future work. |

